# Task 159-002 Execution Plan

## Discovery
- `runEvaluatePhase` in src/orchestra/sprint-phases.ts ALREADY contains the
  PID-bound idempotency guard (Sprint 157 T-002 survivor — commit 6c337b0).
- Helpers in place: `evaluateLockPath`, `isPidAlive`, `tryAcquireEvaluateLock`,
  `releaseEvaluateLock`. Lock file `.deckent/<sprintId>-evaluate-lock` is created
  on entry and unlinked in a `finally` block.
- Behavior verified by reading: same-PID re-entry → NO_OP; live other-PID → NO_OP;
  stale-PID lock → reclaimed; fail-safe on I/O error.
- Missing piece: `tests/orchestra/evaluate-phase-idempotency.test.ts` does NOT
  exist. This task is the test write only — no source-code mutation.

## Plan
1. Create `tests/orchestra/evaluate-phase-idempotency.test.ts` with real-FS
   tmpdir pattern (matching auto-archive.test.ts).
2. Mock heavy dependencies of `runEvaluatePhase` (debt-manager, plugin-hooks,
   result-evaluator, notify, event-stream, sprint-spawner, auditor) so the
   tests focus on lock-file semantics, not full sprint orchestration.
3. Write the canonical 2-parallel-call test plus stale-lock reclaim,
   same-PID re-entry, lock release, and lock payload integrity tests.

## Test Cases
- T1: 2 parallel runEvaluatePhase calls — second is NO_OP, single result set
       (handleEvaluation called exactly once per task across both calls).
- T2: Same-PID re-entry (sequential within process) — second call NO_OP.
- T3: Stale-lock reclaim — dead PID lock allows new caller to acquire.
- T4: Live different-PID lock — new caller is NO_OP (simulated via real PID 1).
- T5: Successful run releases lock — lock file unlinked after call completes.
- T6: Lock payload integrity — file contains pid, startedAt, sprintId.

